v4.5.9
Radon Player 4.5.9: No more cutting in and out at the edge of the truck's range
**Install or update:** `RadonPlayer-Next.apk` (Android), `Radon-Player-4.5.9.msi` (Windows), `radon-player_4.5.9_amd64.deb` (Linux). Each installs over the version you have and keeps your settings and stats.

**What is new**
- **No more cutting in and out at the edge of the truck's range (the phone):** with the truck ignored, every time Android Auto connected or dropped the app changed how the music was kept from it, and each change was a short gap. At the edge of range Android Auto comes and goes again and again, so walking away from the truck or back to it cut the music in and out. Now, while your headphones have the music and the truck is ignored, it's kept from Android Auto the whole time, so Android Auto coming and going changes nothing you hear. Android Auto's map and calls work as before.
- **Ignore Bluetooth devices: no stutter at all:** the Shizuku switch has this name now, and says it's part of Ignore Bluetooth devices, not a setting of its own. It tells you when Ignore Bluetooth devices is off or has no device picked.
- **Problems says more:** every Bluetooth device and Android Auto connecting and disconnecting is noted, so a gap in the sound can be put beside what happened just before.
